<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The Overlord armor's active, granted by the armor's CompProperties_AbilitiesApparel and fed
    by the resurrection core beside it (ThingDefs_Misc/Warcasket_Overlord.xml). Biotech's
    ResurrectionMech (the apocriton's; 1.7.4990, Biotech/Defs/AbilityDefs/Abilities.xml) as a
    VEF ability: the rules live in OverlordWarcasket.Ability_ResurrectMech, the tuning in the
    OverlordWarcasket.ResurrectMechExtension below, both header-documented. Design in
    Docs/Specs/Mech-Resurrection.md.

    The apocriton's numbers, kept where they still mean the same: a 4 second warmup (castTime
    240), a 2 second cooldown (cooldownTime 120; a mod setting), the costs of 1 / 3 / 5
    charges for a light, medium and heavy mech and the 9.9 cell cast range, here the
    distanceToTarget the goto job
    (VFEA_GotoTargetAndUseAbility) walks the pilot to. range is unset on purpose: the click is
    not range-limited, the pilot walks. The sounds, the glow on the mech and the icon are
    Biotech's own (MechResurrect_Warmup, MechResurrect_Cast, MechResurrected,
    UI/Abilities/MechResurrection); Biotech is a hard dependency, so none needs a fallback. The
    two area effects are ours, the apocriton's sized for one mech: OLWC_ResurrectWarmup on the
    corpse through VEF's extension for the length of the warmup and OLWC_ResurrectResolve where
    it lay as the mech stands up (Effects/ResurrectWarmup.xml and ResurrectResolve.xml have the
    sizes).

    The ultraheavy entry, 8 charges, is this ability's own. The apocriton has none, and vanilla
    clears MechWeightClassDef.canResurrect on the class besides, so that a raid's apocriton
    never stands its war queen back up. That rule keeps a boss the player has killed dead; a
    pilot raising the colony's own ultraheavy is what the mech gestator's
    ResurrectUltraheavyMech bill already does for 150 steel. The ability therefore reads this
    table alone and not the flag (Ability_ResurrectMech's header). 8 of the core's 10 charges
    is one ultraheavy a fight with two charges over, where 10 would lock the cast whenever the
    core is short of full, and eight days of recharge or eight advanced components to earn
    back.

    Alpha Mechs' mechs need no entries of their own: every one sits in the four vanilla weight
    classes and leaves an ordinary corpse, so they cost 1 / 3 / 5 / 8 as vanilla's do, its
    boss-size ultraheavies included and its blitzkrieg, a light mech built to blow itself up,
    at a light mech's 1, as an apocriton would raise it. A mech turned by its IFF scrambler
    goes back to the mechanoid faction when it dies
    (HediffComp_DeleteAfterTime.Notify_PawnDied), so its corpse is not the pilot's to raise.

    The corpse window is not the apocriton's: one game day (maxCorpseAgeTicks 60000; a mod
    setting, whose last stop writes 0 here, no limit) against its 1.44 hours (3600 ticks, a real
    minute at normal speed and 20 seconds at triple). That minute suits a raid's apocriton, which
    stands among its mechs, casts by itself the moment one falls and has 30 charges to spend. A
    pilot has to notice the death, walk a warcasket to within cast range and stand through the
    warmup, often from across the map now that the helmet lets the mechs fight there. The window
    is not what limits the ability: the core's charges are, and a longer window spends them no
    faster. A day is the one age the player can read off a corpse, whose inspect pane says "Dead
    for less than a day" until exactly this many ticks have passed, so a mech is resurrectable
    for as long as its corpse says so; the cursor label over a corpse gives the time it has left.

    Single-target, unlike the apocriton's 5 cell area: one cast brings back the one clicked mech,
    so each charge spent is a choice of which mech matters. hasAoE, radius and
    targetingParametersForAoE stay unset (VEF's defaults: no area pickup, no radius ring).

    Targeting: corpse-only parameters with canTargetMechs, which vanilla's corpse rule reads for
    a mechanoid corpse. The faction, the weight class, the window and the charges are decided in
    the ability's CanResurrect, not here, and so is the pilot's bandwidth: the raised mech
    joins the pilot's control group, so the pilot must have room for it (the class header has
    the rule and where vanilla does the same). requireMechlink true: the pilot must be a
    mechanitor; a mod setting.

    showUndrafted true: a mech falls in the workshop too. autocast is pinned off in code; VEF
    never fires an apparel ability's autocast.
  -->
  <VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>
    <defName>OLWC_ResurrectMech</defName>
    <label>resurrect mech</label>
    <description>Resurrect a recently killed mechanoid by externally supercharging its self-repair processes. The mech will come back under the pilot's control with some but not all of its wounds healed, so the pilot needs enough bandwidth for it. Each resurrection costs some of the armor's charges, and heavier mechs cost more.</description>
    <abilityClass>OverlordWarcasket.Ability_ResurrectMech</abilityClass>
    <gizmoClass>OverlordWarcasket.Command_ResurrectMech</gizmoClass>
    <iconPath>UI/Abilities/MechResurrection</iconPath>
    <jobDef>VFEA_GotoTargetAndUseAbility</jobDef>
    <jobReportString>Resurrecting mechs.</jobReportString>
    <targetMode>Thing</targetMode>
    <targetingParametersList>
      <li>
        <canTargetPawns>false</canTargetPawns>
        <canTargetBuildings>false</canTargetBuildings>
        <canTargetItems>false</canTargetItems>
        <canTargetLocations>false</canTargetLocations>
        <canTargetCorpses>true</canTargetCorpses>
        <canTargetMechs>true</canTargetMechs>
      </li>
    </targetingParametersList>
    <distanceToTarget>9.9</distanceToTarget>
    <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
    <castTime>240</castTime>
    <cooldownTime>120</cooldownTime>
    <showUndrafted>true</showUndrafted>
    <warmupStartSound>MechResurrect_Warmup</warmupStartSound>
    <castSound>MechResurrect_Cast</castSound>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="OverlordWarcasket.ResurrectMechExtension">
        <maxCorpseAgeTicks>60000</maxCorpseAgeTicks>
        <costs>
          <li>
            <weightClass>Light</weightClass>
            <cost>1</cost>
          </li>
          <li>
            <weightClass>Medium</weightClass>
            <cost>3</cost>
          </li>
          <li>
            <weightClass>Heavy</weightClass>
            <cost>5</cost>
          </li>
          <li>
            <weightClass>UltraHeavy</weightClass>
            <cost>8</cost>
          </li>
        </costs>
        <appliedEffecterDef>MechResurrected</appliedEffecterDef>
        <centerEffecterDef>OLWC_ResurrectResolve</centerEffecterDef>
        <requireMechlink>true</requireMechlink>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Abilities.AbilityExtension_WarmupEffecter">
        <effecterDef>OLWC_ResurrectWarmup</effecterDef>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef>
</Defs>
